**Form Element Class**

To create a class that represents an individual form element, you can use the following example:

```java
import org.jsoup.nodes.Element;
import org.jsoup.select.Elements;

public class FormElement {
    private String name;
    private String text;

    public FormElement(String name, String text) {
        this.name = name;
        this.text = text;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object o) {
        if (this == o) return true;
        if (o == null || getClass() != o.getClass()) return false;
        FormElement formElement = (FormElement) o;
        return Objects.equals(name, formElement.name) && Objects.equals(text, formElement.text);
    }

    @Override
    public int hashCode() {
        return Objects.hash(name, text);
    }
}
```

This class has two properties: `name` and `text`, which represent the name and text of a form element.

